  "description": "Phase 1549 attested-document envelope corpus. `claims`: build the claim pre-image from the fields, assert byte-equal to `canonical`; `sha256` is the SHA-256 hex of its UTF-8 bytes as a convenience cross-check, and those UTF-8 bytes are EXACTLY what an `ecdsa-p256-sha256-v1` signature covers (base64 IEEE P1363 r||s). `documents`: decode `envelope` against a key directory holding `keys` and assert the verdict named by `expect` (verified / digest-mismatch / signature-invalid / unknown-key). `digest` is the SHA-256 hex of the CANONICAL NODE BYTES of the document, never of the transmitted envelope, so a host recomputes it by decoding the document member and re-encoding it canonically. Field order in the pre-image is pinned; the envelope's own members are Ordinal-sorted per WIRE_FORMAT.md 2. Vectors generated by an independent re-implementation of the encoding written against the normative text; the F# host asserts it reproduces these bytes. See WIRE_FORMAT.md 26.",
